---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro"
import PageIntro from "../components/PageIntro.astro"
const resumeUrl = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}resume.pdf`
---
<BaseLayout title="CV">
  <PageIntro eyebrow="Experience & practice" title="The long version." description="Software engineer working on reliable systems, developer tools, and distributed computing." />
  <div class="cv-page mx-auto max-w-6xl border-t border-[var(--line)] px-6 py-16">
    <div class="mb-14 border-b border-[var(--line)] pb-8">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-extrabold">Mariia (Mary) Feofanova</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-[var(--muted)]">Immigration status: London, SW visa</p>
      <p class="text-[var(--muted)]">Email: <a href="mailto:mary.fifa3000@gmail.com">mary.fifa3000@gmail.com</a></p>
      <p class="text-[var(--muted)]">Open to remote work: yes</p>
      <p class="text-[var(--muted)]">Github: <a href="https://github.com/mary3000">mary3000</a> | LinkedIn: <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/sham42">sham42</a> | Telegram: <a href="https://t.me/sham42">sham42</a></p>
      <a class="mt-6 inline-block border border-[var(--ink)] px-4 py-2 text-sm font-bold" href={resumeUrl} download>Download résumé ↓</a>
    </div>
    <div class="space-y-14">
      <section><h2 class="mb-6 text-2xl font-extrabold">Experience</h2><div class="border-t border-[var(--line)]">
        <article class="border-b border-[var(--line)] py-5"><h3 class="font-bold">Thought Machine London, UK</h3><p class="text-[var(--muted)]">SWE, Ledger, Postings Processing team Aug. 2023 - Now</p><p class="text-[var(--muted)]">GoLang Python Kubernetes Grafana GeminiCLI</p><ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-[var(--muted)]"><li>Developing and maintaining core services responsible for processing and storing financial transactions, balancing high performance with strict consistency.</li><li>Led a team of four engineers to make certain types of transactions traffic more efficient. It resulted in 2x gain in the throughput, proven by internal performance testing.</li><li>Designed a reconciliation tool for the company that helped finding multiple financial consistency bugs. Led a team of two engineers to implement and productionise the tool. After my work proved being useful, it is officially integrated with the product and runs on all environments by default.</li></ul></article>
        <article class="border-b border-[var(--line)] py-5"><h3 class="font-bold">Google LLC London, UK</h3><p class="text-[var(--muted)]">SRE, Cloudnet Control SRE Oct. 2022 - Apr. 2023</p><p class="text-[var(--muted)]">GoLang Borg Monitoring</p><ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-[var(--muted)]"><li>Led a project to migrate a monitoring infrastructure to a new framework. This infrastructure measures ssh connectivity to VMs, and has detected global incidents. The migration enabled the monitoring team to turn off their legacy framework.</li><li>Participated in oncall interrupts shifts.</li></ul></article>
        <article class="border-b border-[var(--line)] py-5"><h3 class="font-bold">Tarantool, Mail.ru Group Moscow, Russia</h3><p class="text-[var(--muted)]">SWE, Tarantool Core team Sept. 2020 - Apr. 2021</p><p class="text-[var(--muted)]">C C++ Lua</p><ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-[var(--muted)]"><li>Was working on the core of Tarantool - an open-source database used by the biggest tech companies in Russia (Mail.ru, Badoo, Mastercard, etc.).</li><li>Improved functionality of indexes: added binary type support for bitset index, implemented option to exclude null values.</li><li>Introduced interactive transactions over the iproto protocol so that now transactions don’t need to be sent in one request.</li></ul></article>
        <article class="border-b border-[var(--line)] py-5"><h3 class="font-bold">JetBrains s.r.o Moscow, Russia</h3><p class="text-[var(--muted)]">SWE, RubyMine team Jul. 2018 - Feb. 2019</p><p class="text-[var(--muted)]">Java Ruby Ruby on Rails</p><ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-[var(--muted)]"><li>Improved refactoring system for RubyMine IDE: developed type specification for extract parameter, added new extraction features, implemented prompt that analyses where to insert missing ”end” keyword.</li></ul></article>
      </div></section>
      <section><h2 class="mb-6 text-2xl font-extrabold">Internships</h2><div class="border-t border-[var(--line)]">
        <article class="border-b border-[var(--line)] py-5"><h3 class="font-bold">Google LLC Remote</h3><p class="text-[var(--muted)]">SWE Internship, Infra Bigtable SRE July 2021 - Sept. 2021</p><p class="text-[var(--muted)]">GoLang Borg</p><ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-[var(--muted)]"><li>I designed, implemented, and tested a prober to monitor the Bigtable backup system. The prober was written in Go, and ran on Google’s cluster management system. It ran continuously to detect backup problems before customers.</li></ul></article>
        <article class="border-b border-[var(--line)] py-5"><h3 class="font-bold">JetBrains s.r.o Remote</h3><p class="text-[var(--muted)]">Research Internship, Programming Languages and Tools Lab July 2020 - Aug. 2020</p><p class="text-[var(--muted)]">C LLVM</p><ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-[var(--muted)]"><li>Modified GenMC model checker (tool for verifying concurrent programs under weak memory models) to test production code: added intrinsics support, sped up allocation instrumentation by more than 2 times.</li><li>Tested mimalloc (Microsoft allocator) using GenMC, designed and implemented 6 tests. Collaborated with mimalloc maintainer Daan Leijen to make mimalloc data-race-free, which resulted in confirming and fixing 6 data races (e.g., wrong memory order). Additionally found 2 tricky bugs which could not be confirmed by other tools.</li></ul></article>
        <article class="border-b border-[var(--line)] py-5"><h3 class="font-bold">Google LLC London, UK</h3><p class="text-[var(--muted)]">SWE Internship, Android App Compat team July 2019 - Sept. 2019</p><p class="text-[var(--muted)]">GoLang Java Android Protobuf SQL</p><ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-[var(--muted)]"><li>Designed and implemented presubmit checker for Android API repository: it analyses API usage statistics and prevents developers from submitting changes that break popular APIs.</li></ul></article>
      </div></section>
      <section><h2 class="mb-6 text-2xl font-extrabold">Projects</h2><div class="border-t border-[var(--line)]"><article class="border-b border-[var(--line)] py-5"><h3 class="font-bold">Model checker for testing concurrent programs [Bachelor thesis] Moscow, Russia</h3><p class="text-[var(--muted)]">C++ TLA+ +Cal Nov. 2019 - May 2020</p><ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-[var(--muted)]"><li>Examined pitfalls of two common concurrency testing techniques (fault injection and verification using +Cal) and created my own solution: model checker that avoids these pitfalls.</li><li>Verified the tool on non-trivial examples. In one of them, my model checker finds complex A-B-A bug 16 times faster than +Cal.</li><li>Made model checker easy to use and understand: it provides an API to create expressive tests and shows steps to reproduce a bug.</li></ul></article></div></section>
      <section><h2 class="mb-6 text-2xl font-extrabold">Teaching Experience</h2><div class="border-t border-[var(--line)]"><article class="border-b border-[var(--line)] py-5"><h3 class="font-bold">Moscow Institute of Physics and Technology Moscow, Russia</h3><p class="text-[var(--muted)]">Teaching Assistant Feb. 2019 - June 2021</p><p class="text-[var(--muted)]">C++ x86 Assembly</p><ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-[var(--muted)]"><li>Theory and Practice of Concurrent Computing: holding seminars and reviewing homework. Learned about internals of modern concurrency concepts from industry, designed new tests for assignments, and contributed to the testing framework by writing model checker as a part of my Bachelor thesis.</li></ul></article></div></section>
      <section><h2 class="mb-6 text-2xl font-extrabold">Achievements</h2><div class="border-t border-[var(--line)]"><article class="border-b border-[var(--line)] py-5"><h3 class="font-bold">Hackathon winner - Photo Lab Live Challenge: Go Viral or Go Home Moscow, Russia</h3><p class="text-[var(--muted)]">Python web.py Heroku Nov. 2018</p><p class="mt-3 text-[var(--muted)]">Developed backend for photo filter that changes the style of clothes. Having only 48 hours was able to quickly learn python web framework and to deploy MVP by collaborating with two teammates.</p></article></div></section>
      <section><h2 class="mb-6 text-2xl font-extrabold">Education</h2><div class="border-t border-[var(--line)]"><article class="border-b border-[var(--line)] py-5"><h3 class="font-bold">Moscow Institute of Physics and Technology Moscow, Russia</h3><p class="text-[var(--muted)]">Bachelor of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science Sept. 2016 - Aug. 2020</p><p class="mt-3 text-[var(--muted)]">Description: Joint degree with the Yandex School of Data Analysis: the most prestigious and selective CS private study program in Russia (∼3% acceptance rate - only 129 students admitted out of ∼4300). It is offered by Yandex, one of the most technologically advanced Russian software companies.</p></article></div></section>
      <section><h2 class="mb-6 text-2xl font-extrabold">Technical Skills</h2><div class="border-t border-[var(--line)] pt-5"><p class="text-[var(--muted)]">Programming Languages: C++, C, GoLang, Java, Python, SQL, TLA+ / +Cal</p><p class="mt-3 text-[var(--muted)]">Knowledge: Algorithms, Data Structures, Databases, Concurrent Computing, Distributed Systems</p></div></section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>